      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## H3 Ripple\n\n1. Upload a video in **Ripple Clip**. Choose the time window, duration and megapixels. Set the crop before editing.\n2. Move anchor 1 to the frame you want to edit. **Download frame**, edit it, then upload, drop or paste the edited image onto its card. Add anchor 2 when another view needs the same change.\n3. **Run**. Ripple Output saves the shot with source audio and a source/result comparison.\n\nThe default is **0.25 MP / 107 frames (4.46 s)**. Duration lists valid frame counts and seconds, up to 3592 frames (149.67 s), limited by the available source video. Upscaling is off by default.\n\nChanging megapixels resizes existing edits. Changing the crop, window or anchor may require a new edit; check the frame card. Keep the full composition of each downloaded frame when editing.\n\nFor local image-model editing, open **H3_Ripple_Local_Editor.json**.\n\n### Models and sampling\nSelect the required model files in the groups below. Start with Ripple LoRA strength 1 and the default Apply prompt. The optional 8-step accelerator is bypassed; set the sampler to 8 steps if you enable it. Keep seeds fixed when comparing edits."
      ],
      "title": "Read me"
    }
